## Where every number comes from

No result in `report.tex` is typed by hand: each is a macro in
`results/numbers.tex`, written by `code/analyze.py` from `results/local/` and
`results/ibex/`. The table (`tables/results.tex`) and figure
(`figures/accuracy.pdf`) are written by the same script.

| In the paper | Macro(s) | Source |
|---|---|---|
| mean accuracies, corrected and naive 95% intervals | `\LRmean \LRlo \LRhi \KNNmean \KNNlo \KNNhi` (+`Naive`) | `results/summary.json` (`logreg`, `knn`) |
| paired difference, intervals, p | `\DIFFmean \DIFFlo \DIFFhi \DIFFloNaive \DIFFhiNaive \DIFFp` | `results/summary.json` (`difference_logreg_minus_knn`) |
| folds LR better / tied / kNN better | `\FoldsLRbetter \FoldsTied \FoldsKNNbetter` | `results/local/folds.csv` |
| chosen k (min, max, median, mode), k grid | `\Kmin \Kmax \Kmedian \Kmode \Kgrid` | `results/summary.json` (`chosen_k_counts`), `code/cv.py` |
| design: 150 flowers, 10 x 5 folds, 50 folds, 120/30, inner 5 folds, seed | `\Nsamples \Nreps \Nfolds \Nouter \Ntrain \Ntest \Ninner \Seed` | `results/*/run_info.json`, `code/cv.py` |
| data checksum | `\DataMD` | `code/data/openml_61_meta.json`, `code/fetch_data.py` |
| LR convergence warnings | `\LRconvWarnings` | `results/*/run_info.json` |
| Ibex node, job id, CPUs (vendors, both x86-64), versions | `\IbexNode \IbexJob \IbexCPU \LocalCPU \NumpyVersion \ScipyVersion \SklearnVersion \PythonVersion` | `results/ibex/ibex_53909243.log`, `results/*/run_info.json` |
| local vs Ibex identical | (text) | `results/summary.json` (`reproducibility`: sha256 of `folds.csv`, `predictions.csv`) |
| k grid 1..30 sensitivity | (text) | `code/README.md` |

Method settings stated in the text (L2, C = 1, lbfgs, Euclidean, uniform
weights, ties to smallest k) are those in `code/cv.py`.

